  {
    "number": 143,
    "title": "Record N30 qualification and keep keyboard A/B outside BUNNY",
    "body": "Keyboard A/B and the attached Super Buttons can be programmed directly on the keyboard. This candidate removes B.U.N.N.Y. requirements to discover, store, edit, dispatch, restore or use them for preset bindings. The corresponding issue definitions (#31, #35, #63–#71) were reconciled while preserving states, metadata and dependencies.\n\nThe qualification report identifies the N30 mouse (85CA), records its four distinct browser outputs, and associates receiver `VID_062A&PID_4101` through the owner's unplug/reconnect inventory. Normal mouse operation was restored. The installed Codex package is `OpenAI.Codex` version `26.917.6896.0`. These results do not qualify native D-pad attribution or a supported Codex-only translation route. The completed personal A=Enter/B=Wispr trial and confirmed mapping restoration remain historical evidence. **#64 remains incomplete and #65 blocked on native mouse qualification.** No keyboard A/B integration gate remains.\n\nMain `79b30c4` is incorporated, including its Depot CI policy. Conflicts were resolved by preserving source history and regenerating affected guide output. No input adapter, installation, personal mapping change or live input dispatch is included in this candidate.\n\nValidation at `99745fa`: Node 24.21.0; workflow validation with 11 current specifications and 13 archives; 15 workflow tests; nine guide maintenance tests; reproducible guide generation; six-width browser, navigation/search and print/PDF checks. All nine diagram artifacts pass 9/9 deterministic checks. The revised N30 viewer passes standalone containment. The preset viewer retains documented vertical overflow without horizontal overflow, so its standalone visual check is not a pass. Refreshed desktop/mobile/print and N30 screenshots were inspected. Guide HTML SHA-256: `cd9e5eb427536332286b6c3798f7ad3f4f3cd4c0224957f9b68563c6a4215ef4`.\n\nIndependent round-4 Standards review approves this comparison. Specification review retains P1 finding SPEC-1 because #64 AC2 still lacks a qualified native four-action route. All six applicable Depot check runs report success through GitHub for the current head; detailed Depot job pages require sign-in and were not inspected. No merge or closure is claimed.\n\nCanonical guide inputs and generated artifacts are synchronized in the PR. Public publication and live qualification remain separate. Only guide UI changed, within the SDLC approval exception. Canonical docs outside the guide require normal CI. No product behavior or contract change requires a new OpenSpec capability.\n\nRefs #64.\n",
